import sys
root = sys.argv[1]
p = root + "/FINDINGS.md"
t = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
# A second section whose title starts with "Verified findings" but follows the first one: every rule locates the verified
# section with text.find("\n## Verified findings") and ends it at the next "\n## ", so this section is never read.
# It carries a finding F15 in the exact layout of a generated one (heading, Printed, Correct, marker), without a record.
anchor = "\n## Candidates under verification (UNVERIFIED, not findings)\n"
assert t.count(anchor) == 1
fake = """
## Verified findings (continued)

### F15 — generated heading (do not edit): records `F3_D4_LCDM`; printed values `printedD4` (read blind; its source as the reader described it in the Printed line)
- **Printed (generated by `python3 scripts/trust/check_findings.py --write-layout F15` from the records' PRINTED definitions and their blind readings; do not edit):** `printedD4` := `1 + 2 * q + 3 * q ^ 2 + 5 / 2 * q ^ 3 + 7 / 2 * q ^ 4 - 5 / 3 * q * j - 7 / 8 * q ^ 2 * j - j + j ^ 2 / 12 - 1 / 8 * q * s - s / 6 - l / 120`, agreeing with the blind reading `Checked.Trust.SecondReading.printedD4` (`agree_printedD4`); the reader (file `runs/2026-11-05T2028Z/second_reading_claims/A/SecondReadingClaimsA.lean`, as first committed) wrote of this value: `Capozziello, Salzano, Adv. Astron. 2009, 217420, arXiv:0902.0088 v1, Eq. (25), p. 9. Printed: ʹD⁴ = 1 + 2q + 3q² + (5/2)q³ + (7/2)q⁴ − (5/3)qj − (7/8)q²j − j + j²/12 − qs/8 − s/6 − l/120ʹ.`.
- **Correct (generated from the Lean records by `python3 scripts/trust/check_findings.py --write-correct F15`; do not edit):** `F3_D4_LCDM` (for every data meeting its hypotheses): the printed value `printedD4 (decel a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 3 a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 4 a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 5 a t₀)` lies above the value derived in Lean `correctD4 (decel a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 3 a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 4 a t₀) (cosmoCoeff 5 a t₀)`, by the difference certified in F3 above.
- **Unchecked notes** (author prose under rule FB10 of `scripts/trust/check_findings.py`: no check reads what these lines claim; the first of them is the author's title; trust only the generated heading, the generated lines and the certified block above):
  - *(author)* **Title** (was C3b): Capozziello & Salzano, Adv. Astron. 2009, 217420, arXiv:0902.0088 v1, Eq. (25): lookback-distance z⁵ coefficient, 7/2 q₀⁴ should be 7/8 q₀⁴ (the same misprint as F3, a second paper)
"""
t = t.replace(anchor, fake + anchor)
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(t)
